{"id":"a25dc870-9673-4255-9341-e4eac166191f","object":"chat.completion","created":1784998636,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    core = case['core_distance']\\n    distances = case['distances']\\n    n = len(nodes)\\n    idx = {node: i for i, node in enumerate(nodes)}\\n    INF = float('inf')\\n    mat = [[INF]*n for _ in range(n)]\\n    for u, v, d in distances:\\n        i = idx[u]\\n        j = idx[v]\\n        w = max(core[u], core[v], d)\\n        mat[i][j] = w\\n        mat[j][i] = w\\n    visited = [False]*n\\n    min_edge = [(INF, None, None) for _ in range(n)]\\n    min_edge[0] = (0, None, None)\\n    mst_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n    for _ in range(n):\\n        u = -1\\n        best = INF\\n        for i in range(n):\\n            if not visited[i] and min_edge[i][0] < best:\\n                best = min_edge[i][0]\\n                u = i\\n        if u == -1:\\n            break\\n        visited[u] = True\\n        w, pu, pv = min_edge[u]\\n        if pu is not None:\\n            mst_edges.append([nodes[pu], nodes[pv], w])\\n            total_weight += w\\n        for v in range(n):\\n            if not visited[v] and mat[u][v] < min_edge[v][0]:\\n                min_edge[v] = (mat[u][v], u, v)\\n    return {'mst_edges': mst_edges, 'total_weight': total_weight}\"}","reasoning_content":"We are given a task: implement solve(case) for DATA-HDB-01. The case payload contains nodes, core_distance (dict mapping node to core distance), and distances (list of triples: [node1, node2, distance]). We need to compute the Minimum Spanning Tree (MST) of a complete graph where edge weights are defined as the mutual reachability distance = max(core_distance[u], core_distance[v], distance(u,v)). Then we need to output the edges of the MST (as list of triples [node1, node2, weight], where weight is the mutual reachability distance), 